issues.problematic_code_snippet:
/* Validate that stored-key to key conversion works correctly */
static int validateStoredKeyConversion(dict *d, const void *key __stored_key) {
    const void *extracted = dictStoredKey2Key(d, key);
    if (d->type->keyFromStoredKey) {
        return extracted != NULL;
    }
    return extracted == key;
}

/* Before the key is released, obtain the link to
 * ensure we can safely access and update the key. */
const void *key = dictStoredKey2Key(d, ptr);
link = dictFindLink(d, ptr, NULL);
serverAssert(link);

/* Setting key of existing dictEntry (newItem == 0)*/

if (*link == NULL) {
    *link = dictFindLink(d, addedKey, NULL);
    assert(*link != NULL);
}

findings.body:
In the `newItem == 0` branch, the new code calls `dictFindLink(d, addedKey, NULL)`. That function expects a lookup key, but `addedKey` is the stored object (or a `keyDup` copy of it). The newly added `dictStoredKey2Key()` conversion is applied in the `newItem == 1` branch but not here. The fix should convert the original key, not the duplicate.

::diff{file="src/dict.c" lines="911-916"}

This is latent. `db.c` always passes a non-NULL link on this path, and hash dicts have no `keyDup` and an identity conversion, so nothing breaks today. But the line was modified in this PR, and a db dict or a `keyDup`-enabled dict reaching the NULL-link branch would hash a `kvobj` as an sds.

::suggestion{file="src/dict.c" lines="914-914"}
        *link = dictFindLink(d, dictStoredKey2Key(d, key), NULL);

`activeDefragHfieldAndUpdateRef()` now computes `key = dictStoredKey2Key(d, ptr)`, but the next line still calls `dictFindLink(d, ptr, NULL)` with the stored `ptr`. The variable is never used, so it's dead code, and it will trigger `-Wunused-variable` under the project's `-Wall`. The code only works because hash dicts have identity conversion, so it looks like the author intended `key` to be used and then didn't finish the change.

::diff{file="src/defrag.c" lines="278-284"}

Either pass `key` to `dictFindLink`, which is the intent of the new line, or drop the conversion and add a comment that the stored `Entry*` is already the lookup key for hash dicts.

`validateStoredKeyConversion()` is defined as `static` but has no callers in the diff or the repo. Under the project's `-Wall`, that triggers `-Wunused-function`. The function is also a weak check: it only asserts the conversion returns non-NULL, or that it is the identity.

::code{file="src/dict.c" lines="101-109"}

Delete it, or wire it into a `debugAssert` where a conversion is actually performed if you want the check.
